["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A clean shot, a fast follow up and cold meat make grouse one of the best meals in the bush. The rules on wings and breasts travel with you all the way home.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two panels. Rimfire on a sitting bird: aim at the head or upper neck. Shotgun on a flying bird: put the pattern on the head and front of the bird, a little ahead of it. Either way aim for the front, where the brain, spine, heart and lungs are.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Where to put the shot</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"42\" width=\"185\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"42\" width=\"185\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">.22, sitting</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Shotgun, flying</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(95 160) scale(1.5 1.5)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"138\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Head, upper neck</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(280 160) scale(1.1 1.1)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#c9a77f\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"318\" cy=\"140\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\" opacity=\".3\"/>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pattern on the head</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">and front, a bit ahead</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aim for the front: brain, spine, heart, lungs.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>.22: head or upper neck. Shotgun: pattern on the head and front (Tip, 70%).</li><li>All the vitals are in the front half <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: shot placement and range</summary><ul><li>Brain, spine, heart and lungs sit in the head, neck and front of the body <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-02\">The body</a>.</li><li>.22 head shots: inside about 25 m (27 yd) for most shooters, with a rest and a dirt backstop (Tip, 55 to 60%).</li><li>Shotgun: most grouse shots are inside about 25 m; improved cylinder and No. 7.5 or 6 lead (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Big game vitals diagrams do not apply to birds; see <a href=\"#/s/shot-placement\">Shot placement</a> for deer.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view. A bird falls near a stump. 1: keep your eyes on the fall spot. 2: pick a mark, the stump, and walk straight to it. 3: search in growing circles around the mark.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bird down: mark it, walk straight</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"260\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You</text>\n<rect x=\"282\" y=\"96\" width=\"14\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><ellipse cx=\"289\" cy=\"92\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"392\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mark: the stump</text>\n<path d=\"M285 150 l10 10 m0 -10 l-10 10\" stroke=\"#c23b22\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"158\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"155\" r=\"24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n<circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"155\" r=\"44\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n<circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"155\" r=\"64\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">1. Eyes on the fall spot</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">2. Walk straight to the mark</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">3. Search in growing circles</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Keep your eyes on the spot, pick a mark, walk straight there (Tip).</li><li>A head shot bird may flap hard on the ground; that is a reflex (Tip, 60%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: reactions and recovery</summary><ul><li>A grouse hit hard falls straight; a wing hit glides or drops and runs (Tip).</li><li>A runner hides under logs, brush and roots. Search slowly in growing circles from the mark (Tip).</li><li>A dog finds wounded birds you will not (Tip).</li><li>Feathers floating but the bird flew on: watch it out of sight; hit birds often land and stay down (Tip).</li><li>Reload, then go. Do not stop to celebrate (Tip).</li><li>Dispatch a live bird quickly and humanely; ask an experienced hunter to show you (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Grouse field care</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 270\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Field care step 1. A grouse with one wing outlined in orange. Note which species it is in the Journal, and leave one feathered wing attached.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"270\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Care 1: tag it in your head</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(140 160) scale(2.2 2.2)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M120 150 q30 -30 70 -10 q-20 30 -70 10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Which species?</text>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Note it in the</text>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Journal.</text>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"167\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">One feathered</text>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">wing stays on.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Note the species. Leave one feathered wing on.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 280\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Field care step 2. A grouse outline: pull the crop at the base of the neck, then make a small cut at the vent and hook out the guts, soon after the shot.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"280\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Care 2: crop and guts out soon</text>\n<path d=\"M60 170 Q70 110 170 105 Q260 100 300 125 L330 108 L360 118 L330 140 Q310 220 200 230 Q90 230 60 170 Z\" fill=\"#efe3cf\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 210 Q200 230 240 205\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Crop: pull it</text>\n<line x1=\"300\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Small cut at the vent, hook out guts</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Pull the crop and the guts soon.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 270\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Field care step 3. Left, crossed: warm birds piled together. Right, ticked: birds spread out in the shade with air around each one. Warm birds in a pile spoil fast, 80 percent.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"270\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Care 3: let the air in</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"185\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c23b22\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"44\" width=\"185\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(90 140) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(106 130) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(120 144) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(100 154) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(250 140) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(310 140) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(370 140) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"66\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#c23b22\"/><path d=\"M164 60 l12 12 M176 60 l-12 12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<circle cx=\"365\" cy=\"66\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M359 66 l4 5 l8 -10\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Piled warm</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spread out, shade</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Warm birds in a pile spoil fast (80%).</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Spread birds out in the shade. No warm piles.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 280\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Field care step 4. A grouse in a cooler with ice, and a thermometer reading under 4 degrees Celsius. At home: fridge up to 3 days, freezer up to 6 months.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"280\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Care 4: cold, fast</text>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"90\" width=\"240\" height=\"140\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<rect x=\"70\" y=\"74\" width=\"260\" height=\"26\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"190\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"170\" y=\"190\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"190\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"280\" y=\"190\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 160) scale(0.7 0.7)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"340\" y=\"90\" width=\"14\" height=\"110\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"347\" cy=\"206\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#c23b22\"/><rect x=\"343\" y=\"150\" width=\"8\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#c23b22\"/>\n<text x=\"347\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Under 4 C</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cooler on ice. Fridge 3 days, freezer 6 months.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Into a cooler on ice, under 4 C.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Cool fast; heat spoils birds <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>One feathered wing stays attached <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the care details</summary><ul><li>Remove the entrails and the crop soon after the kill; food in the crop can sour (80%, Clemson Cooperative Extension).</li><li>Cool quickly; above 4 C (40 F) is the main threat to meat quality <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Wipe the cavity with a clean cloth or paper towel, not grass or snow <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Air around each bird; in hot weather bag each one and keep it on ice; no warm birds piled together <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Transport in a cooler; if none, a ventilated car interior, not the trunk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Note species, MU (Management Unit), date and time in the Journal: Region 3 bag limits are per species <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 296\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two birds. Grouse and quail, and other non migratory game birds: one feathered wing stays attached. Ducks and geese, and other migratory game birds: one feathered wing or the feathered head stays attached. A turkey from a bearded turkey only season also keeps the beard.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"296\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Birds: what stays attached</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"42\" width=\"188\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(100 110) scale(2.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M19 -10 L24 -9 L19 -7 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-14 -4 L-28 -12 L-28 4 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-2 10 L-2 18 M4 10 L4 18\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"104\" r=\"24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse, quail:</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">one feathered</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">wing</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"42\" width=\"188\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(296 110) scale(2.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"15\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2e6b3a\"/><path d=\"M21 -9 L29 -7 L21 -5 Z\" fill=\"#e0a526\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-26 -6 L-22 2 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"90\" r=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<circle cx=\"280\" cy=\"108\" r=\"22\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ducks, geese:</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">one feathered wing</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">OR the feathered head</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Turkey, bearded only season: the beard too.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>One feathered wing stays attached until home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Both breasts are edible portions: take them home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the exact words</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Possession and Transportation, Game Birds, page 15</div><p>\"Anyone who possesses or transports a game bird, other than a migratory game bird, must leave attached to the carcass one feathered wing and for turkey, also the beard, if harvested during a bearded turkey only season.\"</p></aside><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Definitions, page 3</div><p>\"EDIBLE PORTIONS - ... with respect to game birds, means the edible portions of both breasts of the bird.\"</p></aside><ul><li>Breasting in the field: keep the wing attached to the breast you carry (85%, my reading in the <a href=\"#/s/rb-after-the-kill/3\">Rule Book</a>).</li><li>Item 44: you must take the edible portions to your home, a meat cutter or a cold storage plant (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts/18\">Rule Book</a>).</li><li>Possession while hunting or going home: 3 times the daily limit; sharp tailed grouse in Region 3: 2 times (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-bag-limits/5\">Rule Book</a>).</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of meat per bird in grams, hunter estimates, Tip, about 60 percent. Quail 60 to 80. Chukar and partridge 150 to 250. Ruffed grouse 200 to 280. Mallard 350 to 450. Pheasant cock 450 to 600. Canada goose about 1 kilogram of boned breast. A dusky grouse gives about twice a ruffed grouse; a teal is one serving.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Meat per bird, grams (Tip, 60%)</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Quail</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"50\" width=\"13\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"163\" y=\"50\" width=\"4\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"172.8\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">60 to 80</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chukar, partridge</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"90\" width=\"32\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"182\" y=\"90\" width=\"21\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"208.5\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">150 to 250</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Ruffed grouse</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"130\" width=\"42\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"192\" y=\"130\" width=\"17\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"214.8\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">200 to 280</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Mallard</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"170\" width=\"74\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"224\" y=\"170\" width=\"21\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"250.5\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">350 to 450</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Pheasant cock</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"210\" width=\"94\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"244\" y=\"210\" width=\"32\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"282.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">450 to 600</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Canada goose</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"250\" width=\"189\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"339\" y=\"250\" width=\"42\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 1 kg breast</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusky grouse: about twice a ruffed grouse</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"316\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Teal: one serving</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A ruffed grouse gives about 200 to 280 g of meat (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Cook to 74 C (165 F) in the thickest part <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: cooking notes</summary><ul><li>Fridge at 4 C or colder, use within 3 days; freeze at -18 C (0 F), use within 6 months (80%, Clemson).</li><li>Food safety guidance for game birds: 74 C (165 F), checked with a thermometer, since colour is not reliable (80%, extension services citing USDA, the United States Department of Agriculture).</li><li>Grouse breast is lean white meat that dries out fast; many cooks brine it, wrap it, or cook it in a sauce so it stays moist at a safe temperature (Tip).</li><li>Spruce grouse on a needle diet in late fall can taste of pine; brine or braise (Tip).</li><li>Pluck for roasting, skin for speed; the legs are small but worth it (Tip).</li><li>Pick out shot pellets; a pellet hole that looks dark can carry feather bits (Tip).</li><li>More: <a href=\"#/s/cooking\">Cooking wild game</a>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>In short</th><th>Rule Book</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Licence</td><td>Resident: BC hunting licence only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td><td><a href=\"#/s/rb-licences-fees\">Licences</a></td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>1 h before sunrise to 1 h after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td><td><a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/13\">Hours</a></td></tr><tr><td>Tools</td><td>Shotgun, .22, centrefire, air rifle, bow <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td><td><a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/7\">Methods</a></td></tr><tr><td>Roads</td><td>No hunting from vehicles, no loaded gun in one <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td><td><a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts/11\">Items 22, 28</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wing</td><td>One feathered wing stays on <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td><td><a href=\"#/s/rb-after-the-kill/3\">After the kill</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the season and bag table for your regions</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Region</th><th>Grouse season</th><th>Daily bag (possession)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3, MUs 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44</td><td>Youth 1 to 9 Sept; 10 Sept to 30 Nov</td><td>5 each, 10 total (30 total)</td></tr><tr><td>3, MU 3-46</td><td>20 Sept to 30 Nov</td><td>5 each, 10 total</td></tr><tr><td>2, MUs 2-2 to 2-19</td><td>Bow 1 to 9 Sept; 10 Sept to 15 Dec</td><td>10 (30)</td></tr><tr><td>8, MUs 8-1 to 8-15, 8-21 to 8-26</td><td>Youth 1 to 9 Sept; 10 Sept to 30 Nov; bow 1 to 10 Dec</td><td>5 total (15)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>All rows: 99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3/12\">Region 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2/10\">Region 2</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8/10\">Region 8</a>.</li><li>Region 3 footnote: \"For Dusky, Spruce, and Ruffed grouse, the daily aggregate bag limit is 10; the aggregate possession limit is 30.\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Region 8 footnote: \"For Dusky, Spruce, and Ruffed grouse, the daily aggregate bag limit is 5; the aggregate possession limit is 15.\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Road allowance, 400 m single projectile routes, 100 m from buildings: see <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09\">How to hunt</a> and the <a href=\"#/s/rb-where-you-can-hunt/17\">Rule Book</a>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Bird</th><th>Where</th><th>Season</th><th>Bag</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sharp tailed</td><td>Region 3: MUs 3-30, 3-31</td><td>10 Sept to 30 Nov</td><td>5 (10)</td></tr><tr><td>Ptarmigan</td><td>Region 3: 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44</td><td>1 Sept to 30 Nov</td><td>5 (15)</td></tr><tr><td>Ptarmigan</td><td>Region 2: 2-2, 2-3, 2-5 to 2-19</td><td>10 Sept to 15 Dec</td><td>5 (15)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>All 99%, read in the Rule Book. Region 8: no row for either <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the exact words</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Region 3, page 34</div><p>\"There is no open season for sharp-tailed grouse in that portion of MU 3-30 south of the Scottie Creek Forest Service Road (5040 FSR). See Map C18\"</p></aside><ul><li>Region 2 ptarmigan also has a bow only season 1 to 9 September, 5 (15) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Ptarmigan are not open in MU 2-4 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Sharp tailed possession in Region 3 is 2 times the daily limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Sources: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3/12\">Region 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3/20\">Region 3 footnotes</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2/10\">Region 2</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8/10\">Region 8</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fact</th><th>Sure</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>6 grouse: ruffed, spruce, dusky, sooty, sharp tail, ptarmigan</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Ruffed male: unbroken band, 2 rump dots</td><td>70 to 85%</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Young bird: pointed, frayed P9 and P10</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Dusky 0.9 to 1.6 kg; ptarmigan about 350 g</td><td>80 to 85%</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Sooty on the coast, dusky in the Interior</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Sharp tail: about 10,000 breeders in BC (2001), Blue List</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>One way airflow, air sacs as bellows</td><td>80%</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Vitals in the front half</td><td>80%</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Crop stores, gizzard grinds, ceca ferment</td><td>80%</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Spruce grouse: 99% needles in snow season</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Snow roost needs soft snow about 20 cm+</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>3 in 4 chicks die by 5 weeks; about 1 in 2 adults live a year</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>View about 300 degrees, 30 with both eyes</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>No study shows grouse smell hunters</td><td>Tip</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>Flush glide usually under 90 m, often into a tree</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>Harvest 48% near roads vs 19% away</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Families split at about 12 weeks</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>Adults 34% of Oct bag, 57% of Dec bag</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Drum: wings beat air, March to May peak</td><td>75 to 85%</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>Ruffed: 7 to 12 eggs, hatch early June</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>Dusky go uphill to conifers in fall</td><td>70 to 75%</td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>Ptarmigan white by mid October</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>23</td><td>Feed dawn and late day, rest midday</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>24</td><td>Ruffed most common 750 to 1,250 m</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>Young forest under 20 years</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>Track about 5 cm, 3 toes forward, 1 back</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>27</td><td>Hours: 1 h before sunrise to 1 h after sunset</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>.22: grouse, ptarmigan, turkey only</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>29</td><td>Region 3: 5 each, 10 total a day, 10 Sept to 30 Nov</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>Region 8: 5 total a day; Region 2: 10 a day</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>Sharp tail: Region 3 MUs 3-30, 3-31 only</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>No hunting from a vehicle, no loaded gun in it</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>Road allowance: 15 m from the middle (under 3 lanes)</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>FSRs and the road allowance rule: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td>70%</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>One feathered wing on; both breasts home</td><td>99%</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>Cool under 4 C; cook to 74 C</td><td>80%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to use the sheet</summary><ul><li>Screenshot it for the truck.</li><li>Rules rows (27 to 35) come from the app's Rule Book, synopsis 2 October 2026 edition.</li><li>Study aid only. 